// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§4.4", "§18.1"]

// S-264, R-303, F3 of W4-05 U1/b (W4-05 U2): a chain of 1000 aliases `type Ak = (A(k-1), A(k-1))` is
// finished by the check in a short time. The size of Ak is 2^(k+1) - 1 (spec §4.4), so A12 is the
// first to pass 4096 and is the one E0422, at its declaration; the aliases after it use an alias
// that is the error type, so they have no diagnostic, and the signature that writes A12 or the last
// alias has none either (§4.4, §18.1). The error type of an alias is lowered once: the time does
// not double with each alias (it did in 2296e83: 40 aliases took longer than 20 seconds, F3 of
// W4-05 U1/b, and the chain of 1000 did not end).

